# THE NEGATIVE CONTROL for the three tests above: it must pass on BOTH the
# pre-fix and the post-fix build. `s_eventually' over an ordinary signal, and
# over an expression, is legitimate and untouched -- the refusal is conditioned
# on a bare identifier that resolves to a DECLARED property in the same module,
# so a module that merely happens to contain a property declaration does not
# lose the liveness spelling for everything else.
#
# Without this control the three refusals above would be satisfied by a blanket
# rejection of `s_eventually', which would measure nothing.
read_verilog -formal -sv <<EOT
module top (input clk, input req, input ack);
	property p_req_ack;
		@(posedge clk) req |-> ack;
	endproperty
	assert property (s_eventually ack);
	assume property (s_eventually (req && ack));
	assert property (p_req_ack);
endmodule
EOT
# Three concurrent assertions, and NO wire named after the property: the
# named one was expanded rather than left as an undriven identifier. On the
# pre-fix build the same file also passed, which is what makes this a
# control rather than a measurement.
select -assert-count 3 t:$check
select -assert-count 0 w:p_req_ack
select -assert-count 1 t:$logic_and
